        "question_text": "Solve $x^4-2x^3-7x^2+8x+12=0$.",
        "structure": "solve-cubic",
        "solution_text": "1. **Find a factor**\nTest factors of $12$:\n$P(-1)=1+2-7-8+12$\n$=0$\n$(x+1)$ is a factor.\n2. **Divide**\n$x^4\\div x=x^3$\n$(x^4-2x^3-7x^2+8x+12)-x^3(x+1)$\n$=(x^4-2x^3-7x^2+8x+12)-(x^4+x^3)$\n$=-3x^3-7x^2+8x+12$\n$-3x^3\\div x=-3x^2$\n$(-3x^3-7x^2+8x+12)-(-3x^2)(x+1)$\n$=(-3x^3-7x^2+8x+12)-(-3x^3-3x^2)$\n$=-4x^2+8x+12$\n$-4x^2\\div x=-4x$\n$(-4x^2+8x+12)-(-4x)(x+1)$\n$=(-4x^2+8x+12)-(-4x^2-4x)$\n$=12x+12$\n$12x\\div x=12$\n$(12x+12)-12(x+1)$\n$=(12x+12)-(12x+12)$\n$=0$\n$\\therefore P(x)=(x+1)(x^3-3x^2-4x+12)$\n3. **Factorise the quotient**\n$x^3-3x^2-4x+12$\n$=x^2(x-3)-4(x-3)$\n$=(x-3)(x^2-4)$\n$=(x-3)(x-2)(x+2)$\n$\\therefore P(x)=(x+1)(x-3)(x-2)(x+2)$\n4. **Solve**\n$(x+1)(x-3)(x-2)(x+2)=0$\n$\\therefore x=-1,\\ 3,\\ 2,\\ -2$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "$(x-3)$ is a factor of $P(x)=x^3+kx^2+3x-18$. Find $k$, and hence show that $x=3$ is the only real zero of $P(x)$.",
        "structure": "solve-cubic",
        "solution_text": "1. **Find a factor**\n$P(3)=27+9k+9-18$\n$=9k+18$\n$9k+18=0$\n$k=-2$\nSo $P(x)=x^3-2x^2+3x-18$.\n2. **Divide**\n$x^3\\div x=x^2$\n$(x^3-2x^2+3x-18)-x^2(x-3)$\n$=(x^3-2x^2+3x-18)-(x^3-3x^2)$\n$=x^2+3x-18$\n$x^2\\div x=x$\n$(x^2+3x-18)-x(x-3)$\n$=(x^2+3x-18)-(x^2-3x)$\n$=6x-18$\n$6x\\div x=6$\n$(6x-18)-6(x-3)$\n$=(6x-18)-(6x-18)$\n$=0$\n$\\therefore P(x)=(x-3)(x^2+x+6)$\n4. **Solve**\nFor $x^2+x+6$: $\\Delta=(1)^2-4(1)(6)=-23<0$, so it has no real zeroes.\n$\\therefore x=3$ is the only real zero of $P(x)$."
      },
