        "solution_text": "$x^2-9=(x-3)(x+3)$\n$P(3)=81+27-99-27+18$\n$=0$\n$P(-3)=81-27-99+27+18$\n$=0$\n$(x-3)$ and $(x+3)$ are both factors, so their product $(x^2-9)$ is a factor of $P(x)$."
      },
